\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TParticleInsertion
\item[* relevant examples:] turn $\rightarrow$ turn on
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] Verbppropformation
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_
ParticleSpelling
\item[* date of creation:] 19-01-88
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:]--
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To spell out the particle of a verb. \\
For the moment, all particles are placed right behind the verb. A late 
transformation TParticleHop must move the particle over a following 
pronoun, and optionally over a following NP. 
